        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Hardwoods are typically derived from <i>deciduous trees</i> and have complex cellular structures, including vessels (pores). They are generally denser, more durable, and have slower growth rates compared to softwoods, which come from <i>coniferous trees</i> and lack vessels. Examples of hardwoods include mahogany and odum, while softwoods include pine and spruce.</p>",
